s+=tex(r'c_r=\sqrt{\binom{12}r}x_r,\qquad q=\sum_{r=0}^{12}\binom{12}r|x_r|^2,\qquad P_9=q^2S_9(\psi/\sqrt q).')
s+=tex(r'\boxed{q^2\left('+B+r'q^2-P_9\right)=\sum_B\sum_{m=0}^{2L_B}\frac{\mathbf v_{B,m}^{\dagger}G_B\mathbf v_{B,m}}{\binom{2L_B}{m}}\ge0.}')
s+='<p>The polynomial vectors have degree four; all rational Gram matrices are symmetric and positive definite. Division by q to the fourth power proves the upper bound for every nonzero complex state. The independent verifier derives the sector polynomial from reduced density matrices, expands the complete identity and checks positive leading principal minors exactly.</p>'
