s+='<p><a href="basis.json" download>Polynomial vectors ↓</a> · <a href="sos-certificate.json" download>Exact matrices and scales ↓</a> · <a href="independent-verification.json">Verification report and input hashes</a></p><p>Variable indices 0–12 denote the binomial-scaled amplitudes; 13–25 denote their conjugates. Divide each polynomial channel by its basisScales factor before applying its matrix.</p></section><section class="reference-section" id="verify"><h2>Reproduce the proof</h2><pre>python3 verify_certificate.py</pre><p>The <a href="verify_certificate.py">standalone verifier</a> uses exact arithmetic. It runs with the Python standard library; installing python-flint optionally accelerates the same exact matrix and polynomial checks.</p></section>'
